A||||3||wayne||radiator problems
Z||000000||wayne||06-11-99||05:56 AM||||I have a 85 GT. the problem I'm having is the overflow tank for the radiator fills up and overflows. Of course this means no water back in the engine for cooling. I let some water out of the overflow and reserviced the engine from the back. I ran the engine for about 5 minutes and shut it down. Water rushed into the overflow tank again. I replaced the radiator cap and it seemed to do ok for a day or so and them it did it again. Any suggestions.<p>wayne 
Z||000001||theogre||06-11-99||12:07 PM||||try it w/o the thermostat. if it stops then the thermostat may need replacement. if it continues do a dry compression test on all cyls. you may have a blown head gasket. if the dry test looks close on all cyles, try a wet test just to be sure. The wet test will reduce ring leakaage to make the test read better.<p>the wet test is done by spraying some oil into the cyl. don't just pour it in, the oil likely won't cover well. <p>I usually put a bit of plastic tube on a syringe and push the tube into the cyl, with the piston most of the way to the top. the tubing needs to be stiff enough to reach the far wall of the cylinder so the oil will get all the way around the rings. Other wise it just lays on the low side and doesn't give a true result. You only need a couple CC's of oil. 
Z||000002||wayne||06-11-99||06:34 PM||||thanks for your reply. I'll check it out<p>I have another question.<p>I've had problems with this car burrning up catiltic converters. My state has an emmision check I have to deal with every year. This time I put a new converter on and will take it back out as soon as i pass the test.<p>This is a lot of trouble, do you have any suggetions why it burns them up. i went throught 3 in about a 4 month period.<p>wayne 
Z||000003||theogre||06-11-99||06:46 PM||||a rich running motor, oil burning, and antifreeze leaking into the motor, will all cause problems like that.
